   "text": "I read the structure region by region and wrote it as a SMILES string.\n\n- **Quinazoline core:** C4 carries the piperazine N, C2 carries the NH chain, C6 has Cl, C7 has the aryl group and C8 has F.\n- **Piperazine:** the second N bears C(=O)CH(OH)\u2082, which is drawn as the dihydroxyacetyl (hydrate) group.\n- **Aryl group:** a 2-fluoro-6-hydroxyphenyl ring. The hashed bonds on its ring look like drawing artifacts, so I assigned no stereo there.\n- **Linker:** NH\u2013CH\u2082CH\u2082\u2013C(=O)\u2013N(CH\u2083)\u2013CH\u2082CH\u2082 followed by five O\u2013CH\u2082CH\u2082 units, with the last one ending in OCH\u2082C(=O)NH. I counted five ether oxygens in the drawing.\n- **tert-Leucine:** the wedge on the N\u2013C\u03b1 bond gives S, which is the natural L configuration.\n- **Hydroxyproline:** the wedged carboxamide at C2 gives S, and the hashed OH at C4 gives R, so this is the natural (2S,4R) form.\n- **Benzylic amine:** the wedged methyl gives S for the CH(CH\u2083) attached to the 4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)phenyl ring.\n\nI derived each @/@@ tag from the CIP assignment above rather than copying a known compound.\n\nSMILES: OC(O)C(=O)N1CCN(CC1)c1nc(NCCC(=O)N(C)CCOCCOCCOCCOCCOCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N2C[C@H](O)C[C@H]2C(=O)N[C@@H](C)c2ccc(cc2)-c2scnc2C)nc2c(F)c(c(Cl)cc12)-c1c(O)cccc1F"
